    <div class="article-body">

        <p>Listing your items might feel overwhelming at first, but this guide will walk you through your options and help you choose the best setup for your inventory.</p>

        <hr />

        <h2>Before you start: Weigh items accurately</h2>

        <p>Your item's weight determines its shipping cost — so it's crucial to enter the correct weight when listing.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Underestimating weight</strong> → The carrier may return the package to you.</li>
            <li><strong>Overestimating weight</strong> → Buyers may overpay for shipping.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="article-info-box">
            <strong>Tip:</strong> Use a scale. When in doubt, it's better to <strong>round up</strong> slightly than under-report.
        </div>

        <hr />

        <h2>Types of listings on Lively</h2>

        <p>When creating a listing, you'll first choose between two formats:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Temporary Listings</strong>
                <ul>
                    <li>Only visible during the live show in which they're created</li>
                    <li>Disappear when the show ends</li>
                    <li>Fast to create with minimal details</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Quality Listings</strong>
                <ul>
                    <li>Stay active even after the show ends</li>
                    <li>Require detailed descriptions and photos</li>
                    <li>Ideal if you want long-term visibility for your items and/or carry items from one show to the next</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
        </ul>

        <p>Each listing, whether Temporary or Quality, can also be set as the following:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Auction</strong>
                <ul>
                    <li>Price increases as viewers bid</li>
                    <li>Runs for a set duration</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Buy-It-Now (BIN)</strong>
                <ul>
                    <li>Fixed price</li>
                    <li>Available throughout the show and beyond (if it's a Quality Listing)</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
        </ul>

        <p>Additional options for BIN listings only:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#">Accept Offers</a> - Let buyers submit offers on BIN listings</li>
            <li><a href="#">Flash Sales</a> - Temporarily discount BIN items during a show — only available for Quality Listings.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Most sellers use a mix of Auction and BIN listings in their shows; this combination offers buyers more ways to shop.</p>

        <hr />

        <h2>Shipping settings for your first show</h2>

        <p>When creating listings, simply choose a Shipping Profile that reflects the item's weight (from the dropdown menu). <strong>If your item is in between weights, choose the higher weight to avoid under-reporting the weight and risk having the carrier send the item back to you.</strong></p>

        <hr />

        <h2>Which listing format should you use?</h2>

        <h3>✓ Selling a handful of unique items you want to show off one-by-one?</h3>
        <p>Use <strong>Quality Listings</strong> with clear photos and descriptions. You can list each as an Auction or a BIN.</p>

        <h3>✓ Selling a high volume of items, many of which are similarly weighted?</h3>
        <p>Use <strong>Temporary Listings</strong> grouped by weight.</p>
        <p>For example, if you're auctioning off 100 items that weigh between 1 and 2 kilograms, you can do the following:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Create a listing titled "1–2 kilos"</li>
            <li>Set quantity to 100</li>
            <li>Keep "List these products individually" turned off</li>
            <li>As you run items, Lively will auto-label items as "1–2 kilos #1," "1–2 kilos #2," etc.</li>
            <li>Use sticky notes or labels as you run the items to track which item corresponds to which number</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This method is great for high-volume or randomized inventory.</p>

        <h3>✓ Selling a high volume of items and want to create a Quality Listing for each item?</h3>
        <p>Try our <a href="#">CSV uploader.</a></p>

        <h3>✓ Running a card break?</h3>
        <p>Use our <a href="#">Breaks Feature.</a></p>

        <h3>✓ Running a Surprise Set?</h3>
        <p>Use our <a href="#">Surprise Sets Feature.</a></p>

